From: Ritesh Raj Sarraf <rrs@debian.org>
Subject: [PATCH] cosmic-store: build with the packagekit backend

The COSMIC Store is built flatpak-only by default (its `packagekit` feature is
off), so on stock Debian it has no apt data source and can sit on "Loading...".
Build it with `--features packagekit` so the store lists Debian packages (via
AppStream) alongside Flatpak apps, like GNOME Software.
--- a/justfile
+++ b/justfile
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ build:
     cd cosmic-settings && {{ just }} build-release
     cd cosmic-settings-daemon && {{ just }} build-release
     {{ just }} cosmic-session/build-release
-    {{ just }} cosmic-store/build-release
+    {{ just }} cosmic-store/build-release --features packagekit
     {{ just }} cosmic-term/build-release
     {{ just }} cosmic-viewer/build-release
     {{ make }} -C cosmic-wallpapers all
